•The tax rules applicable to “fast-pay stock” could result in adverse consequences to preferred stock holders;
•Our level and terms of indebtedness could adversely affect our ability to raise additional capital;
•If we are unable to service our indebtedness, we could default and face bankruptcy or liquidation;
•We may be unable to fund cash settlements or repurchases of our outstanding convertible notes, and any future debt may limit our ability to engage in cash settled conversions or repurchases of convertible notes;
•Despite our current level of indebtedness, we may incur substantially more indebtedness and enter into other transactions in the future which could further exacerbate the risks related to our indebtedness.
